{"uid":"ebd7ceb93c4e33b4","name":"test_one_extra_key_is_named_exactly_once_on_a_subprocess_stderr","fullName":"tests.test_structured_findings#test_one_extra_key_is_named_exactly_once_on_a_subprocess_stderr","historyId":"a0c1233ce1a255c39cd0a971cb18eefb","time":{"start":1791881020972,"stop":1791881021155,"duration":183},"description":"Task 014 (requirement E.1, #190): \"one warning\" as an ordinary\n    process observes it -- under Python's DEFAULT warning and logging\n    configuration, not a test harness's capture. Validating one otherwise\n    valid finding carrying one unrecognised key writes that key's name to\n    stderr exactly once, on exactly one line. This is the shape that\n    caught the two-channel revision (`warnings.warn` plus a\n    `logger.warning` of the same text: two stderr lines, two occurrences\n    of `future_key` for one key), so it is pinned here.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 014 (requirement E.1, #190): &quot;one warning&quot; as an ordinary<br />\nprocess observes it -- under Python's DEFAULT warning and logging<br />\nconfiguration, not a test harness's capture. Validating one otherwise<br />\nvalid finding carrying one unrecognised key writes that key's name to<br />\nstderr exactly once, on exactly one line. This is the shape that<br />\ncaught the two-channel revision (<code>warnings.warn</code> plus a<br />\n<code>logger.warning</code> of the same text: two stderr lines, two occurrences<br />\nof <code>future_key</code> for one key), so it is pinned here.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795115,"stop":1791880795116,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795116,"stop":179188079